{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.FlavorSplitHabiroDerivation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.FlavorSplitHabiroDerivation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NoncommRing"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FlavorSplit.alternating_projection_weak_vertex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FlavorSplit.alternating_projection_weak_vertex","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/flavor-split-habiro-derivation.lean#L124-L138","doc":"The $H_4$ alternating representation evaluation of the weak vertex insertion.\nIn the alternating (sign) channel representing left-handed fermions, the Hecke\ngenerator evaluates to its alternating eigenvalue: σ = -q⁻¹.\nThus, the 2-vertex insertion σ⁻² evaluates to q².\nThis theorem formalizes that this insertion expands exactly as 1 + h·q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FlavorSplit.topological_flavor_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FlavorSplit.topological_flavor_split","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/flavor-split-habiro-derivation.lean#L105-L122","doc":"The commutative specialisation, kept under its original name so that\ncitations do not move. Now **derived** from\n`topological_flavor_split_of_central` rather than proved separately: in a\ncommutative ring every element is central, and the right inverse `h_inv1`\nis retained only for signature compatibility — the proof does not use it.\n\nThe `unusedVariables` linter is silenced on this declaration deliberately:\nthe warning it emits IS the finding — `h_inv1` was a hypothesis of the\noriginal statement and is never needed — so it is recorded here rather\nthan removed by dropping the binder, which would move the signature. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:flavor-split-habiro-derivation","label":"conj:flavor-split-habiro-derivation","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/flavor-split-habiro-derivation.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FlavorSplit.topological_flavor_split_of_central","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FlavorSplit.topological_flavor_split_of_central","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/flavor-split-habiro-derivation.lean#L51-L102","doc":"**The flavour split over an arbitrary ring, with `h` central.**\n\nIn any ring in which the Hecke quadratic `σ² = hσ + 1` holds, `h` is\ncentral, and `σ` has a **left** inverse, the difference between the proton\nbraid `σ³` and the neutron braid `σ⁻³` is the scalar `h(h² + 3)`.\n\nCommutativity of the ambient ring is not needed — which matters, because\nH_n(q) does not have it for n ≥ 3, while `h = q - q⁻¹` is a scalar and so\nis central there. Nor is a right inverse: given the quadratic, a left\ninverse already forces `σ⁻¹ = σ - h`.\n\nThe proof routes through the *conjugate* quadratic `σ⁻² = 1 - hσ⁻¹`\nsatisfied by the mirror generator, then reads each cubic off its own\nquadratic. Centrality is used at exactly one step, squaring `σ - h`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}